<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed flat at 1.49 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed flat at 1.49 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.2235 to the dollar, down from 3.2205 on Tuesday and at 1.8785 to the mark, up from 1.8805, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.49 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, nearly flat from Tuesday's 1.48 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
